  "id": "DrugBank_DB01030 - MONDO_6045",
  "verbalization": "Topotecan is implicated in the pathogenesis of Ovarian Clear Cell Adenocarcinoma through a chain of indications involving Altretamine. The evidence suggests that Topotecan may act as a precursor or mediator in the development of this cancer, as it is linked to several adenocarcinoma subtypes, including Ovarian Adenocarcinoma and Ovarian Mucinous Adenocarcinoma, all of which are indicated to interact with Altretamine. This suggests a potential pathway where Topotecan may influence the progression or maintenance of these malignancies, possibly through shared molecular mechanisms or by promoting the expression of genes that are targets of Altretamine. The recurring involvement of Altretamine in this chain implies a possible role in the biological processes that underlie Ovarian Clear Cell Adenocarcinoma, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a hypothesis that Topotecan may contribute to the development of this cancer through indirect interactions, possibly via the activation of pathways that are also engaged by Altretamine.",
